From c862c92daf79cc65925e3dca43d28e8695a52bad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Wen <jackwen04@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:02:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] kk: Add transform feedback buffers, counters and
 queries

Bound buffers and the active transform feedback stream queries go to the
GS's geometry parameters. The buffer offsets live in 4 dwords of the
command buffer's pool, which vkCmdBeginTransformFeedbackEXT loads from the
counter buffers given (zero otherwise) and vkCmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT
stores to them, through a copy kernel.

A VK_QUERY_TYPE_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM_EXT query has two reports,
primitives written then needed, which the pre-GS program adds to between
vkCmdBeginQueryIndexedEXT and vkCmdEndQueryIndexedEXT. Reports are now
addressed by the query stride, and only occlusion queries remap their
index.

The GS count pass and pre-GS program now only run while transform
feedback or one of its queries is active: otherwise nothing fits in the
buffers and nothing is counted anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
